From: rdndds <rdndds@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 29 Apr 2026 15:00:29 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] NetBpfLoad: treat non-optional program load failures as non-fatal

A failed load of a program not marked optional logs an error but falls
through, so the enclosing loop returns a failure for the code section and
bpfloader exits non-zero. With "reboot_on_failure reboot,bpfloader-failed"
on the service, that reboots the device.

On a 4.14 kernel several programs cannot be loaded regardless of what the
loader does, so aborting gains nothing. Log a warning and continue.

Aborting provides no recovery path here: the failing programs are
unsupported by the kernel, so every boot would hit the same exit.

Signed-off-by: rdndds <rdndds@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/bpf/loader/NetBpfLoad.cpp b/bpf/loader/NetBpfLoad.cpp
index 48ca600..cf88d92 100644
--- a/bpf/loader/NetBpfLoad.cpp
+++ b/bpf/loader/NetBpfLoad.cpp
@@ -1051,7 +1051,9 @@ static int loadCodeSections(const char* elfPath, vector<codeSection>& cs, const
                           cs[i].name.c_str());
                     continue;
                 }
-                ALOGE("non-optional program %s failed to load.", cs[i].name.c_str());
+                ALOGW("non-optional program %s failed to load, continuing anyway",
+                      cs[i].name.c_str());
+                continue;
             }
         }
 
